Short answer
- Find the column index whose label string matches your label, then read the cell value at that (row, col) with wxGrid::GetCellValue(row, col).

Detailed, practical approach (with ready-to-use code)
1) Simple linear search (best for small/medium grids, simplest to implement)

C++:
```cpp
wxString GetCellValueByColumnLabel(wxGrid* grid, const wxString& colLabel, int row)
{
    if (!grid) return wxEmptyString;
    const int cols = grid->GetNumberCols();
    const int rows = grid->GetNumberRows();
    if (row < 0 || row >= rows) return wxEmptyString; // or throw/error

    for (int c = 0; c < cols; ++c)
    {
        if (grid->GetColLabelValue(c) == colLabel)   // exact match
        {
            return grid->GetCellValue(row, c);
        }
    }
    return wxEmptyString; // label not found
}
```

Variants / improvements:
